the top three blocks are all `444/848/444`.\n- The blocks in the middle column below the top row are also A copies.\n- Every other block is solid 8.\n\n**The other pairs.**\n- Pair 1 follows the same rule: block (0,0) is `393/393/333` (A in 3 on 9), and block (0,2) is solid 9 because B[0][2] is empty.\n- Pair 3 uses 4×4 shapes and gives a 16×16 output. Its first block is `7777/8878/8788/7777`, which is A drawn in 7 on 8.\n\n**Test input.** A and B are both 5×5, cropped to the bounding box of their non-zero cells. The output will be 25×25: A drawn in colour 3 wherever B is set, and solid 4 elsewhere.\n\n**Construction stages emitted by the program:**\n1. Allocate the output filled with c4.\n2. Stamp one A block for each filled cell of B, one emit per row of B.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    pans = panels(g)\n    crops = []\n    for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in pans:\n        p = crop(g, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n        ys, xs = np.nonzero(p != bg)\n        crops.append(p[ys.min():ys.max()+1, xs.min():xs.max()+1])\n    A, B, P3, P4 = crops[:4]\n    c3 = int(P3[0, 0]); c4 = int(P4[0, 0])\n    ha, wa = A.shape\n    hb, wb = B.shape\n    out = np.full((hb * ha, wb * wa), c4, dtype=int)\n    emit(out, f\"Allocate a {hb*ha}x{wb*wa} canvas (B's grid of A-sized blocks) filled with colour {c4}.\")\n    tile = np.where(A != bg, c3, c4)\n    for i in range(hb):\n        stamped = False\n        for j in range(wb):\n            if B[i, j] != bg:\n                out[i*ha:(i+1)*ha, j*wa:(j+1)*wa] = tile\n                stamped = True\n        if stamped:\n            emit(out, f\"Row {i} of shape B: stamp shape A (colour {c3} on {c4}) in every block where B is filled.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each input is split by grey (5) columns into four panels:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How the output is built (checked against all three pairs).** The output is a grid of blocks, and each block is the size of A."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp one A block for each filled cell of B, one emit per row of B."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Row 0 of shape B: stamp shape A (colour 3 on 9) in every block where B is filled."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Row 1 of shape B: stamp shape A (colour 3 on 9) in every block where B is filled."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Test input.** A and B are both 5×5, cropped to the bounding box of their non-zero cells."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a 9x9 canvas (B's grid of A-sized blocks) filled with colour 9."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a 9x9 canvas (B's grid of A-sized blocks) filled with colour 8."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"116a0b9efa58e278faa1477cd01f84df17fc1895803ac92b681b83057be7a012","task_sha256":"499a43ed8fe9b0f21cefd864ce67d878186979cbd6841de44e7056ddd8e9e7e9","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
